---
import SectionTitle from "./SectionTitle.astro";
---

<section id="about" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
  <SectionTitle kicker="A bit of context" title="About me" />

  <div class="flex max-w-[68ch] flex-col gap-4 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <p>
      I work in a team of three, which means I own what I ship: the design decisions, the delivery
      and the consequences. It taught me early that the interesting part of a feature is rarely the
      code — it's the schema underneath it and what happens when the data grows.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of my time goes into backend and data: Django REST APIs, PostgreSQL, query plans, indexes
      and moving expensive work off the critical path. Recently I've spent it on the parts that only
      show up under load — connection pooling, backpressure, autoscaling that does what you think it
      does — and on getting an LLM to do something genuinely useful inside a product.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've just finished an MSc in Software Development &amp; Architecture at La Salle (URL). I'm
      interested in systems that have to hold up: data design, performance, and decisions that still
      make sense two years later.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
